# ─── Spendify Android configuration ───────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the backend URL the packaged app should
# call. This value is baked into the JS bundle at build time (`npm run build`),
# so re-run the build + `npx cap sync android` after changing it.
#
# A phone/emulator CANNOT reach your PC's localhost. Pick the right target:
#   • Android emulator  → http://10.0.2.2:4000     (emulator's alias for your PC)
#   • Real phone (Wi-Fi)→ http://192.168.x.x:4000   (your PC's LAN IP)
#   • Production        → https://your-deployed-backend.example.com
#
# Leave empty to use same-origin '/api' (only works for the web build behind a
# proxy — not for the native Android app).
VITE_API_URL=
